1
00:00:00,524 --> 00:00:03,083
Sir, field report number one on the electricity

2
00:00:03,123 --> 00:00:03,540
file.

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,292
Today's subject:

4
00:00:04,332 --> 00:00:05,794
electricity itself.

5
00:00:05,834 --> 00:00:06,808
The stuff in the wire.

6
00:00:06,848 --> 00:00:07,839
What is it, exactly?

7
00:00:07,879 --> 00:00:09,107
This whole planet runs on it.

8
00:00:09,147 --> 00:00:12,123
Lights, phones, factories, hospitals.

9
00:00:12,477 --> 00:00:13,737
Cut it for one hour..

10
00:00:13,777 --> 00:00:15,882
and their civilization stands in line.

11
00:00:15,936 --> 00:00:17,306
Strangest thing I found:

12
00:00:17,346 --> 00:00:19,446
what runs in their wires moves slower than

13
00:00:19,486 --> 00:00:20,248
a snail.

14
00:00:20,288 --> 00:00:22,063
Yet the lamp lights instantly.

15
00:00:22,103 --> 00:00:22,666
So how?

16
00:00:22,706 --> 00:00:24,108
What is a volt, anyway?

17
00:00:24,148 --> 00:00:25,375
And why do they have two kinds of

18
00:00:25,415 --> 00:00:26,080
electricity..

19
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,645
that they fought over, all the way to

20
00:00:27,685 --> 00:00:28,834
the electric chair?

21
00:00:28,964 --> 00:00:31,398
It began about twenty-six hundred years ago.

22
00:00:31,438 --> 00:00:33,104
A Greek rubbed a lump of amber on

23
00:00:33,144 --> 00:00:33,800
some fur..

24
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:35,826
and it started pulling feathers and straw.

25
00:00:35,866 --> 00:00:37,112
The Greek word for amber:

26
00:00:37,152 --> 00:00:37,856
Elektron.

27
00:00:37,896 --> 00:00:39,789
That gave them the word Electricity.

28
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:41,467
Their most important invention..

29
00:00:41,507 --> 00:00:42,631
named after a rock.

30
00:00:42,671 --> 00:00:45,149
Then for two thousand years, nobody understood it.

31
00:00:45,189 --> 00:00:45,823
They rubbed..

32
00:00:45,863 --> 00:00:46,554
and watched.

33
00:00:46,594 --> 00:00:47,229
What happened:

34
00:00:47,269 --> 00:00:49,159
everything here is made of atoms.

35
00:00:49,199 --> 00:00:51,493
Around every atom are very tiny things called

36
00:00:51,533 --> 00:00:52,335
electrons.

37
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:54,180
They carry something called charge.

38
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,055
Negative charge.

39
00:00:55,095 --> 00:00:56,762
The heart of the atom is positive.

40
00:00:56,802 --> 00:00:57,663
The rule is simple:

41
00:00:57,703 --> 00:00:58,754
opposites attract.

42
00:00:58,794 --> 00:00:59,257
Likes..

43
00:00:59,297 --> 00:01:00,444
push apart.

44
00:01:00,484 --> 00:01:01,464
Just like humans, sir.

45
00:01:01,504 --> 00:01:03,342
Except electrons don't hire lawyers.

46
00:01:03,382 --> 00:01:05,552
When the Greek rubbed the amber, electrons jumped

47
00:01:05,592 --> 00:01:06,703
from the fur to the stone.

48
00:01:06,743 --> 00:01:07,454
It had extra..

49
00:01:07,494 --> 00:01:09,121
so it pulled anything light nearby.

50
00:01:09,161 --> 00:01:11,017
They call that static electricity.

51
00:01:11,057 --> 00:01:13,366
Charge piling up somewhere, with no way out.

52
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:14,973
A human walks across a carpet..

53
00:01:15,013 --> 00:01:16,066
and gets charged.

54
00:01:16,106 --> 00:01:17,046
Touches a doorknob..

55
00:01:17,086 --> 00:01:18,055
the charge jumps.

56
00:01:18,095 --> 00:01:18,569
Spark.

57
00:01:18,609 --> 00:01:20,818
That little spark is thousands of volts.

58
00:01:20,858 --> 00:01:22,394
But almost no charge behind it.

59
00:01:22,434 --> 00:01:23,403
It just stings.

60
00:01:23,443 --> 00:01:24,911
Now scale that spark up..

61
00:01:24,951 --> 00:01:25,382
lightning.

62
00:01:25,422 --> 00:01:26,305
A charged cloud.

63
00:01:26,345 --> 00:01:27,514
The charge leaps down.

64
00:01:27,554 --> 00:01:28,399
A typical bolt:

65
00:01:28,439 --> 00:01:30,589
about three hundred million volts.

66
00:01:30,629 --> 00:01:32,465
And about thirty thousand amps.

67
00:01:32,505 --> 00:01:34,588
Lightning hits this planet dozens of times..

68
00:01:34,628 --> 00:01:35,697
every second.

69
00:01:35,737 --> 00:01:37,422
One bolt heats the air around it to

70
00:01:37,462 --> 00:01:39,546
five times the surface of the sun.

71
00:01:39,586 --> 00:01:40,845
And the boom they hear after..

72
00:01:40,885 --> 00:01:42,061
is the air bursting.

73
00:01:42,101 --> 00:01:44,607
In seventeen fifty-two, an American named Franklin said

74
00:01:44,647 --> 00:01:47,207
lightning is electricity, and proposed an experiment to

75
00:01:47,247 --> 00:01:47,615
prove it.

76
00:01:47,655 --> 00:01:49,576
A year later, a scientist in Russia tried

77
00:01:49,616 --> 00:01:49,816
it..

78
00:01:49,856 --> 00:01:50,504
and died.

79
00:01:50,544 --> 00:01:52,329
So humans learned lesson one early:

80
00:01:52,369 --> 00:01:53,495
electricity kills.

81
00:01:53,535 --> 00:01:54,156
No warning.

82
00:01:54,196 --> 00:01:56,549
But charge that sits still powers nothing.

83
00:01:56,589 --> 00:01:58,621
What does the work is moving charge.

84
00:01:58,661 --> 00:01:59,647
That's called current.

85
00:01:59,687 --> 00:02:02,026
A copper wire is full of loose electrons.

86
00:02:02,066 --> 00:02:03,900
To get moving they need two things:

87
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:05,419
a push, like a battery.

88
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:07,432
And a closed path that brings them back

89
00:02:07,472 --> 00:02:08,103
to the start.

90
00:02:08,143 --> 00:02:08,920
A circuit.

91
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:09,791
Close the switch..

92
00:02:09,831 --> 00:02:12,248
the circuit is complete, the electrons move, and

93
00:02:12,288 --> 00:02:13,116
the lamp lights.

94
00:02:13,156 --> 00:02:14,420
Now the riddle from the start.

95
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,072
The electron itself crawls:

96
00:02:16,112 --> 00:02:17,685
under a millimeter per second.

97
00:02:17,725 --> 00:02:18,640
The snail wins.

98
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,905
But the push races around the circuit near

99
00:02:20,945 --> 00:02:22,169
the speed of light.

100
00:02:22,243 --> 00:02:22,711
Why?

101
00:02:22,751 --> 00:02:24,170
The wire is already full.

102
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:25,403
Like a hose full of water:

103
00:02:25,443 --> 00:02:26,081
open the tap..

104
00:02:26,121 --> 00:02:27,878
water comes out the far end at once.

105
00:02:27,918 --> 00:02:29,083
Not the water you put in.

106
00:02:29,123 --> 00:02:30,386
The water already waiting there.

107
00:02:30,426 --> 00:02:31,200
Open the switch..

108
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,479
the circuit breaks, and everything stops.

109
00:02:33,519 --> 00:02:35,059
The whole wire, all at once.

110
00:02:35,099 --> 00:02:37,752
So their light switch doesn't send electricity.

111
00:02:37,792 --> 00:02:38,801
It's a drawbridge.

112
00:02:38,841 --> 00:02:40,003
Up, or down.

113
00:02:40,229 --> 00:02:42,090
And if electrons find a shortcut with no

114
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:42,555
lamp?

115
00:02:42,595 --> 00:02:44,495
They all rush through, the wire heats up

116
00:02:44,535 --> 00:02:45,485
and burns.

117
00:02:45,525 --> 00:02:46,370
A short circuit.

118
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:48,508
So every house has a breaker that trips

119
00:02:48,548 --> 00:02:50,182
when the current gets too high.

120
00:02:50,325 --> 00:02:52,166
Materials come in two kinds.

121
00:02:52,206 --> 00:02:54,661
Metals like copper have loose electrons, so they

122
00:02:54,701 --> 00:02:55,347
conduct.

123
00:02:55,387 --> 00:02:57,676
Plastic and rubber hold theirs tight, so they

124
00:02:57,716 --> 00:02:58,280
insulate.

125
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,716
That's why every wire wears a jacket.

126
00:03:00,756 --> 00:03:03,854
To understand electricity, humans compare it to water.

127
00:03:03,894 --> 00:03:05,332
A tank on the roof, a pipe coming

128
00:03:05,372 --> 00:03:05,687
down.

129
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,502
The higher the tank, the harder the water

130
00:03:07,542 --> 00:03:08,136
pushes.

131
00:03:08,176 --> 00:03:10,590
In electricity, that push is called the volt.

132
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:12,244
How much water flows through the pipe each

133
00:03:12,284 --> 00:03:12,906
second..

134
00:03:12,946 --> 00:03:14,012
that's the current.

135
00:03:14,052 --> 00:03:15,161
Measured in amps.

136
00:03:15,201 --> 00:03:16,964
If the pipe has a narrow spot, less

137
00:03:17,004 --> 00:03:17,938
water gets through.

138
00:03:17,978 --> 00:03:19,154
That's resistance.

139
00:03:19,194 --> 00:03:20,285
Measured in ohms.

140
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:21,334
Raise the tank..

141
00:03:21,374 --> 00:03:22,896
more pressure, more flow.

142
00:03:22,936 --> 00:03:24,870
The exact same law in a wire.

143
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:27,008
The work that water can do, push times

144
00:03:27,048 --> 00:03:27,553
flow:

145
00:03:27,593 --> 00:03:28,654
that's the watt.

146
00:03:28,694 --> 00:03:30,155
The thing they pay for on the bill.

147
00:03:30,195 --> 00:03:32,122
A modern bulb draws about ten watts.

148
00:03:32,162 --> 00:03:33,831
A kettle, about two thousand.

149
00:03:33,871 --> 00:03:34,617
One cup of tea..

150
00:03:34,657 --> 00:03:35,846
two hundred bulbs.

151
00:03:35,886 --> 00:03:37,801
The old bulb had a thin wire inside,

152
00:03:37,841 --> 00:03:39,369
with high resistance on purpose.

153
00:03:39,409 --> 00:03:41,140
The electrons jam up in it, and it

154
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:42,478
heats until it glows.

155
00:03:42,518 --> 00:03:43,852
So their light used to be..

156
00:03:43,892 --> 00:03:44,645
a traffic jam.

157
00:03:44,685 --> 00:03:46,260
These units are all people.

158
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,901
Volta, Italian, built the first battery in eighteen

159
00:03:48,941 --> 00:03:49,846
hundred.

160
00:03:49,886 --> 00:03:50,875
Ampère, French.

161
00:03:50,915 --> 00:03:51,776
Ohm, German.

162
00:03:51,816 --> 00:03:52,944
And Watt, Scottish.

163
00:03:52,984 --> 00:03:54,656
Every one of these scientists died..

164
00:03:54,696 --> 00:03:56,286
and their name ended up on a bill.

165
00:03:56,326 --> 00:03:57,253
Their highest honor.

166
00:03:57,293 --> 00:03:58,204
To picture the numbers:

167
00:03:58,244 --> 00:04:00,396
a phone charger puts out about five volts.

168
00:04:00,636 --> 00:04:01,397
A wall socket:

169
00:04:01,437 --> 00:04:03,674
one-ten to two-forty, depending on the country.

170
00:04:03,714 --> 00:04:04,508
High power lines:

171
00:04:04,548 --> 00:04:05,884
hundreds of thousands.

172
00:04:05,924 --> 00:04:06,519
Lightning:

173
00:04:06,559 --> 00:04:07,878
hundreds of millions.

174
00:04:07,918 --> 00:04:08,685
A note for command:

175
00:04:08,725 --> 00:04:10,949
an ordinary wall socket is enough to kill

176
00:04:10,989 --> 00:04:11,557
a human.

177
00:04:11,597 --> 00:04:13,444
What hurts is the current that passes through

178
00:04:13,484 --> 00:04:14,084
the body.

179
00:04:14,124 --> 00:04:15,715
And their bodies conduct.

180
00:04:15,818 --> 00:04:17,876
Why is current so dangerous to them?

181
00:04:17,916 --> 00:04:19,896
Because they run on electricity themselves.

182
00:04:19,936 --> 00:04:22,759
Their nerves carry orders as tiny electric pulses.

183
00:04:22,799 --> 00:04:24,752
Their heart beats because an electric pulse tells

184
00:04:24,792 --> 00:04:25,185
it to.

185
00:04:25,225 --> 00:04:25,794
Every beat.

186
00:04:25,834 --> 00:04:28,299
A stray current scrambles the heart's own signal.

187
00:04:28,339 --> 00:04:30,308
Like someone yelling into a phone call.

188
00:04:30,441 --> 00:04:32,068
Some creatures use it as a weapon.

189
00:04:32,108 --> 00:04:33,713
A fish in South American rivers:

190
00:04:33,753 --> 00:04:35,684
in twenty nineteen they measured its shock at

191
00:04:35,724 --> 00:04:37,600
eight hundred sixty volts.

192
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,272
And when Volta built the first battery, he

193
00:04:39,312 --> 00:04:40,384
was copying that fish.

194
00:04:40,424 --> 00:04:42,075
So the planet's first battery..

195
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,317
was a counterfeit fish.

196
00:04:43,357 --> 00:04:45,382
Current comes in two kinds.

197
00:04:45,422 --> 00:04:45,906
One:

198
00:04:45,946 --> 00:04:46,619
direct.

199
00:04:46,659 --> 00:04:49,177
The electrons flow one way, all the time,

200
00:04:49,217 --> 00:04:49,890
like a river.

201
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:51,462
That's what comes out of any battery.

202
00:04:51,502 --> 00:04:52,133
Short name:

203
00:04:52,173 --> 00:04:52,800
DC.

204
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:53,240
Two:

205
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:53,974
alternating.

206
00:04:54,014 --> 00:04:56,112
The electrons go back and forth in place.

207
00:04:56,152 --> 00:04:57,758
Back and forth, like a saw.

208
00:04:57,798 --> 00:04:58,471
Short name:

209
00:04:58,511 --> 00:04:59,707
AC.

210
00:04:59,747 --> 00:05:01,720
It flips direction fifty or sixty times a

211
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,307
second.

212
00:05:02,347 --> 00:05:03,446
Depends on the country.

213
00:05:03,597 --> 00:05:04,909
The lamp lights either way.

214
00:05:04,949 --> 00:05:06,995
Going out, the electrons heat the wire..

215
00:05:07,035 --> 00:05:08,546
coming back, they heat it too.

216
00:05:08,586 --> 00:05:09,968
A saw cuts both ways.

217
00:05:11,159 --> 00:05:13,917
So why would anyone want back-and-forth electricity?

218
00:05:13,957 --> 00:05:15,662
The answer, sir, is a fight.

219
00:05:15,702 --> 00:05:17,088
One of this planet's most famous.

220
00:05:17,128 --> 00:05:20,275
In eighteen eighty-two, Thomas Edison opened the first

221
00:05:20,315 --> 00:05:22,411
power station in New York.

222
00:05:22,451 --> 00:05:24,598
Direct current, one hundred ten volts.

223
00:05:24,638 --> 00:05:26,128
On day one it lit about four hundred

224
00:05:26,168 --> 00:05:26,603
lamps.

225
00:05:26,643 --> 00:05:28,010
But it had one big flaw:

226
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:29,561
its power couldn't reach farther than about a

227
00:05:29,601 --> 00:05:30,760
kilometer and a half.

228
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,492
After that the pressure drops and the wire

229
00:05:32,532 --> 00:05:33,114
heats up.

230
00:05:33,154 --> 00:05:35,063
So every neighborhood needed its own station.

231
00:05:35,103 --> 00:05:36,521
A coal plant on every street.

232
00:05:36,561 --> 00:05:37,332
A great plan..

233
00:05:37,372 --> 00:05:38,559
for coal sellers.

234
00:05:38,599 --> 00:05:40,613
Then came an immigrant from Europe named Nikola

235
00:05:40,653 --> 00:05:41,169
Tesla.

236
00:05:41,209 --> 00:05:43,546
He reached America in eighteen eighty-four.

237
00:05:43,586 --> 00:05:44,982
Worked for Edison a few months..

238
00:05:45,022 --> 00:05:46,299
they clashed, and he left.

239
00:05:46,339 --> 00:05:48,438
He had designs for motors and generators running

240
00:05:48,478 --> 00:05:49,790
on alternating current.

241
00:05:49,830 --> 00:05:52,554
A businessman named Westinghouse bought the inventions.

242
00:05:52,795 --> 00:05:55,241
AC had one advantage, and it changed everything:

243
00:05:55,281 --> 00:05:56,970
you can raise its pressure to thousands of

244
00:05:57,010 --> 00:05:59,149
volts with a simple device called a transformer,

245
00:05:59,189 --> 00:06:00,724
send it hundreds of kilometers..

246
00:06:00,764 --> 00:06:02,145
and step it back down before it enters

247
00:06:02,185 --> 00:06:02,663
the house.

248
00:06:02,703 --> 00:06:03,668
Details in the next report.

249
00:06:03,708 --> 00:06:04,968
Edison didn't sit still.

250
00:06:05,008 --> 00:06:07,148
From eighteen eighty-eight he ran a fear campaign:

251
00:06:07,188 --> 00:06:08,438
AC is a killer.

252
00:06:08,478 --> 00:06:10,618
His men electrocuted animals in front of reporters

253
00:06:10,658 --> 00:06:12,585
to prove it.

254
00:06:12,625 --> 00:06:14,304
In eighteen ninety, New York State carried out

255
00:06:14,344 --> 00:06:16,568
the first execution in the electric chair.

256
00:06:16,608 --> 00:06:17,910
The man who built the chair ran it

257
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:20,551
on Westinghouse generators, of all things, bought behind

258
00:06:20,591 --> 00:06:21,128
his back.

259
00:06:21,168 --> 00:06:24,047
So the name AC would stick to death.

260
00:06:24,087 --> 00:06:26,425
The execution itself was gruesome and slow.

261
00:06:26,465 --> 00:06:27,561
Westinghouse said afterward:

262
00:06:27,601 --> 00:06:29,000
they would have done better with an axe.

263
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:30,683
When humans compete for a market..

264
00:06:30,723 --> 00:06:31,784
there are no limits.

265
00:06:31,824 --> 00:06:33,032
But the math won.

266
00:06:33,072 --> 00:06:35,715
In eighteen ninety-three, Westinghouse lit the entire Chicago

267
00:06:35,755 --> 00:06:37,431
World's Fair with AC.

268
00:06:38,198 --> 00:06:40,297
And in eighteen ninety-six, power from Niagara Falls

269
00:06:40,337 --> 00:06:41,555
reached the city of Buffalo..

270
00:06:41,595 --> 00:06:43,396
more than thirty kilometers away.

271
00:06:43,949 --> 00:06:44,826
Thirty kilometers.

272
00:06:44,866 --> 00:06:46,596
Edison topped out at one and a half.

273
00:06:46,636 --> 00:06:47,206
Fight over.

274
00:06:47,246 --> 00:06:49,276
Since then, the grid across the whole planet

275
00:06:49,316 --> 00:06:50,729
is alternating current.

276
00:06:50,769 --> 00:06:52,101
From the station to the socket.

277
00:06:52,141 --> 00:06:53,002
But wait, sir.

278
00:06:53,042 --> 00:06:55,308
Any device with a screen or a battery..

279
00:06:55,348 --> 00:06:57,625
runs on direct current inside.

280
00:06:57,665 --> 00:07:00,183
The phone, the computer, the modern bulb, the

281
00:07:00,223 --> 00:07:02,110
solar panel, the electric car.

282
00:07:02,150 --> 00:07:03,111
And the little cube at the end of

283
00:07:03,151 --> 00:07:04,074
the charger cable?

284
00:07:04,114 --> 00:07:06,463
Its whole job is turning wall AC into

285
00:07:06,503 --> 00:07:07,017
DC.

286
00:07:07,057 --> 00:07:09,453
So every home holds twenty tiny peace treaties

287
00:07:09,493 --> 00:07:10,727
between Edison and Tesla.

288
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:12,611
And the longest power lines on the planet

289
00:07:12,651 --> 00:07:13,036
today..

290
00:07:13,076 --> 00:07:13,987
are direct current.

291
00:07:14,027 --> 00:07:16,257
In China, a line went live in twenty

292
00:07:16,297 --> 00:07:16,298
nineteen.

293
00:07:16,338 --> 00:07:18,489
About three thousand three hundred kilometers long.

294
00:07:18,529 --> 00:07:20,923
At one point one million volts.

295
00:07:20,963 --> 00:07:23,980
Because over very long distances, with modern electronics,

296
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,249
DC loses less.

297
00:07:25,289 --> 00:07:27,134
So after a hundred and forty years, the

298
00:07:27,174 --> 00:07:28,239
score is a tie.

299
00:07:28,279 --> 00:07:29,441
Nobody told Edison.

300
00:07:29,619 --> 00:07:31,665
Two words from the human dictionary.

301
00:07:31,705 --> 00:07:32,913
AC and DC:

302
00:07:32,953 --> 00:07:34,422
alternating and direct.

303
00:07:34,462 --> 00:07:36,267
They also named a very loud band after

304
00:07:36,307 --> 00:07:36,978
them.

305
00:07:37,018 --> 00:07:38,158
And kilowatt-hour:

306
00:07:38,198 --> 00:07:40,327
a thousand watts running for one full hour.

307
00:07:40,367 --> 00:07:41,899
The unit they get billed in every month.

308
00:07:41,939 --> 00:07:43,123
Report summary, sir.

309
00:07:43,163 --> 00:07:43,496
One:

310
00:07:43,536 --> 00:07:44,844
electricity is charge.

311
00:07:44,884 --> 00:07:47,107
Sitting still, it's static; moving, it's current.

312
00:07:47,147 --> 00:07:47,479
Two:

313
00:07:47,519 --> 00:07:49,928
the volt is pressure, the amp is flow,

314
00:07:49,968 --> 00:07:51,673
the ohm is the squeeze.

315
00:07:51,725 --> 00:07:52,217
Three:

316
00:07:52,257 --> 00:07:54,666
AC travels far, DC runs the devices.

317
00:07:54,706 --> 00:07:55,950
And the two live together.

318
00:07:56,165 --> 00:07:56,993
One last warning:

319
00:07:57,033 --> 00:07:58,474
electricity is no toy.

320
00:07:58,514 --> 00:08:00,021
If you haven't studied it, don't open a

321
00:08:00,061 --> 00:08:02,097
device, and keep away from bare wire.

322
00:08:02,137 --> 00:08:03,443
Leave it to trained people.

323
00:08:03,571 --> 00:08:04,253
Next report:

324
00:08:04,293 --> 00:08:05,772
where is electricity made?

325
00:08:05,812 --> 00:08:07,215
And how does it travel from a station

326
00:08:07,255 --> 00:08:08,735
hundreds of kilometers away..

327
00:08:08,775 --> 00:08:10,330
to a socket in the wall, in the

328
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:11,229
same instant?

329
00:08:11,269 --> 00:08:12,282
This was Earth Report.

330
00:08:12,322 --> 00:08:13,008
Agent Peek.

331
00:08:13,048 --> 00:08:14,169
Transmission ends.
